{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7722","id":5211993189,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABNqi0ZQ","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7722","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7722.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7722.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7722","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7722/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7722/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7722/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/3017caba8d0b16cd448e271bddd17bb108e4ec94","number":7722,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"design(id): #2043 extension — three currencies, supply account, pending-unit trading","user":{"login":"developing-today[bot]","id":347365078,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOFLRe1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/developing-today","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\n- Adds a design-extension document for the three modifications in Drew's 2026-11-08 rulings on the #2043 design (titled \"ID currencies v1\" on the issue — the units are tokens, not currencies; see doc §0) (rulings already recorded on #2043 and #2296 — this PR does not change them, and does not change the settled base design in `doc/2026-11-01_design_id2043.md`).\n- **Three token classes** (Q1): units / pending units / revoked units on one ledger as a **double-entry** structure — three token classes as account classes, a chart of accounts, a journal-entry table for every life-cycle event, and invariants restated in double-entry terms (per Drew's follow-on ruling \"double entry\", 2026-11-08 09:13 CST; §1 rewritten in commit 5ce3af3d22, superseding the first draft's two-readings fork and balance-classes recommendation).\n- **Supply account** (Q2): defines the supplying account, mint/burn accounting, and replacement wording for Invariant 2. The phrase \"named like tiger beetle would be\" is carried UNRESOLVED, verbatim, uninterpreted.\n- **Pending-unit trading** (#2296, Q5): full mechanics — chained option contracts from the initial grant, the originator cancel option (1:1 pending → revoked, 14 days from Init), the option contract as a required client input (trades without one are denied), the 28-day notAfter auto-sign, chained redemption ordering, and the exact rewording #2296's Decision 2 needs so \"pending never spendable\" survives tradability. Drew's atomic batch escrow idea is designed as an option with a recommendation — it is his open proposal (his text ends with \"?\"), not a ruling.\n- Ends with an UNRESOLVED list (U1–U6; U7 was answered by the double-entry ruling and is removed with a disposition note) quoting each unclear phrase verbatim with the specific clarification needed, ready to lift into a questions batch.\n- **Terminology — tokens, not currencies** (Drew, 2026-11-08 09:26 CST; commit 3017caba8d): new doc §0 — the units are **tokens** (representations of grants and capabilities for a server or a world; no value by definition — WoW gold / LoL RP / Robux analogies). \"Currency\" survives only as TigerBeetle's term: TigerBeetle `ledger` = one token system, and the base design's \"currency\" reads as \"token\" (the base doc is not rewritten). Terminology pass over the extension doc's prose; `currency.*` event-type identifiers and the currency-service name unchanged. Consequence notes per section: DE invariants unchanged, issuance reframed as entitlement issuance, trades transfer entitlements and \"consideration\" never prices the token.\n- **Future extensions — deferred, with seams** (doc §6; approved by Drew 2026-11-08 09:27 CST on the condition that nothing in v1 blocks maintaining and transitioning the system): the six known gaps (anchored provisioning for user-created token systems, a backend dimension on the binding, cross-backend atomicity, ledger-type migration, per-token policy fields, U6 blocking escrow Variant E), each with the seam v1 leaves and its transition path; the two current narrowings (§1's one-TigerBeetle-ledger-per-programme, §3 windows as global constants) are named in §6.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `git diff --check` clean. Docs-only; no implementation tests run.\n\nRefs #2043\nRefs #2296\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796738963&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7722&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7722&signature=6abcc22b47e548b97958bd463f870bac2ac4d603f9748270993d41eb70a83d8e\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source medi